MzcwMDM3OTI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symfony/symfony/labels/Status:%20Needs%20Review","name":"Status: Needs Review","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2020-12-01T09:19:24Z","updated_at":"2020-12-01T14:00:24Z","closed_at":"2020-12-01T14:00:24Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Symfony version(s) affected**: 5.2.0\r\n*5.2-RC2 was not affected*\r\n\r\n**Description**  \r\n\r\nUsing the new authenticator-based security,\r\nand a custom authenticator (which extends `AbstractAuthenticator`),\r\nusers get this error after login: `Call to a member function getUserLoader() on null`\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/919405/100719957-9d8c8680-33bd-11eb-8303-403210a65571.png)\r\n\r\nThis is caused by `PasswordMigratingListener`, being triggered automatically since #39213, to assume than every Passport contains an UserBadge. This is nor documented ([here](https://symfony.com/doc/current/security/experimental_authenticators.html)) nor enforced by `UserPassportInterface`, so I believe it should be tested.\r\n\r\n**How to reproduce**  \r\n\r\n/ \r\n\r\n**Possible Solution**  \r\n\r\nPR coming soon\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"romaricdrigon","id":919405,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxOTQwNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/919405?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romaricdrigon","html_url":"https://github.com/romaricdrigon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romaricdrigon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romaricdrigon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romaricdrigon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https: